<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34739" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-crĕpo</span></b> , ŭi,
			ĭtum, 1, v. a. and n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to sound very
			much</i>, <i>to resound</i>, <i>ring</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lucum percrepare vocibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 13, § 31</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to make resound</i>, <i>to celebrate loudly</i>: pugnam, Lucil. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 255, 14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
